<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-10">10 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">HMS Dreadnought is launched</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">King Edward VII launched the battleship at Portsmouth. With ten 12-inch guns and steam turbines, she made existing battleships obsolete and intensified the naval race with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/april-18">18 April</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Earthquake and fire devastate San Francisco</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A magnitude 7.9 earthquake struck before dawn, and fires burned for three days. Some 3,000 people died and more than half the city's population was left homeless.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-22">22 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Wright brothers receive their patent for a flying machine</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The US Patent Office granted Orville and Wilbur Wright patent 821,393 for their method of controlling an aircraft. They spent years defending it in the courts.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/bambatha-rebellion" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bambatha-rebellion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/bambatha-rebellion">Bambatha Rebellion</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Bambatha Rebellion was a Zulu uprising against British rule and taxation in the Colony of Natal in 1906, sparked by a new poll tax.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/first-battle-of-bud-dajo">First Battle of Bud Dajo</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The First Battle of Bud Dajo, also called the Moro Crater massacre, was an American assault in March 1906 on Tausug Muslims who had taken refuge in the crater of the volcano Bud Dajo on Jolo in the southern Philippines.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Battle</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rawdat-muhanna">Battle of Rawdat Muhanna</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Battle of Rawdat Muhanna was fought in April 1906 in the Qassim region of central Arabia between Abd al-Aziz ibn Saud and Abd al-Aziz ibn Mutib, emir of Jabal Shammar.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Revolt</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/satiru-uprising">Satiru uprising</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Satiru uprising was a Mahdist rising in 1906 at the village of Satiru near Sokoto, in the Protectorate of Northern Nigeria.</p></div></li></ol></section>
